  <section|Argument correspondence><label|argument-correspondence>

  The off-origin scalar identity <verbatim|eq:ex-lattice-shell-green> is the
  explicit induction corresponding to <verbatim|YM.Extra.FD.shell_green> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Extra/FREE_DETECTOR_ALGEBRA/Harmonic.lean>:
  <verbatim|applyDiff_succ> decomposes the normalized Taylor coefficient into
  derivatives of frozen first-slot tensors; the trace sum vanishes by
  <verbatim|freeze_trace>, and their coordinate contraction recovers the
  original tensor by <verbatim|freeze_diagonal>. The trace vanishing is
  derivative-slot harmonicity: differentiating the Bianchi identity and
  summing gives <verbatim|Delta F_im=0> after the divergence terms vanish;
  the coefficient/freeze relation then gives <verbatim|sum_a
  partial_a(A_a)=0>. It is not inferred from the Maxwell divergence equation
  alone. The response formula in <verbatim|eq:ex-lattice-kelvin-response>
  then groups radial Green differentiation, divergence reduction, and the
  second curl in <verbatim|reply_radial> and <verbatim|curl_kelvin>. The
  manuscript supplies this radial calculation explicitly: the divergence-free
  equation removes derivatives of the field strength, the radial-curl
  identity gives the factor <verbatim|j+2>, and the derivative of
  <verbatim|\|x\|^{-2(j+2)}> gives the reflected radial term. Its constant is
  <verbatim|strength j = 4(j+1)(j+2)(-2)^j normal>, with
  <verbatim|normal=1/(4*pi^2)>.

  The translated Taylor maps in the manuscript are <verbatim|towards j k
  (-I(x))> with the source normalization <verbatim|strength(j)/strength(k)>.
  Their finite sum is <verbatim|field_expands>. Applying the Kelvin response
  termwise gives the signal of <verbatim|Shift.signal_kelvin>.
  <verbatim|invert_line>, <verbatim|line_eq>, and <verbatim|signal_diag>
  justify the line-jet statement: the first nonzero normalized Taylor
  coefficient is at order <verbatim|j> and equals <verbatim|strength(j)
  rr(x)^(j+2) solO(face x) P>. The one-leg test formula <verbatim|replyTest>
  supplies the second-side sign <verbatim|(-1)^k>.

  The reflection in <verbatim|scan>/<verbatim|legKernel> is
  <verbatim|solO(face x)>, which acts on both the field indices and every
  derivative slot. This is the full action <verbatim|(s dot
  Q)(v)=s^(2)Q(sv)>, not merely a two-index matrix multiplication. The
  manuscript's lower-triangular transform on the finite direct sum of
  solution grades is the source <verbatim|shiftAll>. <verbatim|newLeg_below>
  makes its off-diagonal blocks vanish after using the symmetry of
  <verbatim|towerB>; <verbatim|newLeg_diag> and <verbatim|slide_top> give the
  diagonal factor <verbatim|(-1)^j strength(j) rr(x)^(j+2) dotF(P,Q)>. Since
  this factor is positive and <verbatim|dotF> is positive definite,
  <verbatim|towerB_pos> proves positivity on the full tower simultaneously.
  The manuscript additionally explains invertibility from the identity
  diagonal and strict grade lowering.

  For a finite orthogonal basis of this tower, <verbatim|aligned_step> is the
  exact removal identity. The manuscript solves its recurrence by induction
  on monomial degree, obtaining the diagonal weight <verbatim|prod_i alpha_i!
  d_i^(alpha_i)>. <verbatim|from_large> represents every fixed Wick
  polynomial in a sufficiently large finite tower. The manuscript explains
  why: every restricted linear jet coordinate is represented by a vector in
  the finite-dimensional solution space via its Frobenius Riesz vector, so a
  polynomial in finitely many jet coordinates is a finite polynomial in tower
  coordinates. Thus <verbatim|reflected_positive> is strict on every nonzero
  Wick polynomial.

  <verbatim|shellSector> is the image of the polynomial observation map, so
  quotienting by Maxwell's equations and Bianchi relations is not an informal
  deletion of coordinates. <verbatim|no_residual> uses <verbatim|point_probe>
  and strict positivity to show that no further on-shell vector is invisible
  to every probe; <verbatim|free_null> identifies the free field quotient
  with the kernel of the observation map. <verbatim|writes_inj> embeds that
  quotient into the polynomial algebra. Finally, <verbatim|faceTest_eq>
  identifies the actual scanner columns with the reflected pairing, applying
  the geometric reflection to every tensor index and ordinary coefficient
  conjugation separately. Strict positivity then gives
  <verbatim|scanner_inj>.

  <section|Literature search and scope><label|literature-search-and-scope>

  The shared literature index <verbatim|blueprint/background/README.md> and
  the background notes were searched for an accepted all-grade Kelvin/Maxwell
  detector or matching theorem. No directly applicable reviewed result was
  found. This manuscript therefore gives the local derivation and the finite
  algebraic recurrence rather than attributing them to an unverified external
  reference. No external result is invoked in the proof. The mathematical
  linear-algebra facts used are finite-dimensional Gram--Schmidt and the
  finite-dimensional inverse of a lower-triangular matrix with identity
  diagonal; their use is spelled out in the prose.

  <section|Commands and checks><label|commands-and-checks>

  Targeted source navigation used <verbatim|rg -n> for the declarations in
  the table and <verbatim|sed -n> on the listed files, especially the full
  proofs of <verbatim|reply_radial>, <verbatim|signal_kelvin>,
  <verbatim|shiftAll_gram>, <verbatim|towerB_pos>, <verbatim|aligned_step>,
  <verbatim|aligned_script>, <verbatim|duplex_script>,
  <verbatim|reflected_positive>, <verbatim|no_residual>, and
  <verbatim|scanner_inj>. The repository background index was read. No Lean
  build, theorem check, or LaTeX build was run. Running <verbatim|python3
  scripts/check_blueprint.py> failed because the isolated clone does not
  contain the coordinator-owned <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json>.
  No Lean build, theorem check, or LaTeX build was run.

  <section|Remaining proof/review questions><label|remaining-proofreview-questions>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Check the exact map from the source's shell-sector quotient to the
    gauge-invariant field-strength grades used in the integrated manuscript.

    <item>Independently review the finite-moment removal recurrence and
    scanner interpretation; this unit proves only the free reference
    detector, not any interacting positivity or comparison estimate.
  </itemize-minus>

